\title{Representation and size}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2026-01-15}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Given a concept class #{\mathcal{C}_n} of #{X_n}, and an alphabet #{\Sigma}, a \em{representation} of #{\mathcal{C}_n} by #{\Sigma} is a function #{\mathcal{R} \colon \Sigma^* \to \mathcal{C}_n}.}

\p{Given a representation #{\mathcal{R}} and a concept #{c \in \mathcal{C}_n} we define}

##{\operatorname{size}(c) = \operatorname{length}(\text{shortest word } w \text{ for which } \mathcal{R}(w) = c).}
